           <item>
            <widget class="QLabel" name="names_info_label">
             <property name="text">
              <string>&lt;b&gt;Why the names matter&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;In many tools, you add the PSG files, and Snooz looks for the accessory file of each one in the same folder, with the same name. For example, the accessory file of subject01.edf is subject01.tsv.</string>
             </property>
             <property name="textFormat">
              <enum>Qt::TextFormat::RichText</enum>
             </property>
             <property name="wordWrap">
              <bool>true</bool>
             </property>
            </widget>
           </item>
          </layout>
         </widget>
        </item>
        <item>
         <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="about_renaming_layout">
          <property name="spacing">
           <number>6</number>
          </property>
          <item>
           <widget class="QLabel" name="about_renaming_title_label">
            <property name="font">
             <font>
              <bold>true</bold>
             </font>
            </property>
            <property name="text">
             <string>About the renaming</string>
            </property>
           </widget>
          </item>
          <item>
           <widget class="QLabel" name="about_renaming_label">
            <property name="text">
             <string>&lt;b&gt;The order of the rules&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Snooz applies the rules to the name of each file, without its extension, in this order.&lt;br/&gt;• "Pattern to remove". Every occurrence of the pattern is removed.&lt;br/&gt;• "Characters to keep". Only the first characters of the name are kept.&lt;br/&gt;• "Prefix". It is added at the start of the name.&lt;br/&gt;• "Suffix". It is added at the end of the name.&lt;br/&gt;Then the extension is put back.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Example&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The file subject01_annotations_v2.tsv, with the pattern _annotations, 9 characters to keep and the prefix visit1_.&lt;br/&gt;• Without the pattern, the name is subject01_v2.&lt;br/&gt;• With its first 9 characters, it is subject01.&lt;br/&gt;• With the prefix, the new file is visit1_subject01.tsv.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Which files are renamed&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• With an extension in "File extension", only the files of the list with this extension are renamed. The other files are left as they are.&lt;br/&gt;• With an empty "File extension", all the files of the list are renamed.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;The new files&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• Snooz copies or renames each file, as set in "Keep the original file".&lt;br/&gt;• Two files of the list must not get the same new name, for example with too few characters to keep. The second one would replace the first.&lt;br/&gt;• The log lists each file copied or renamed.</string>
            </property>
            <property name="textFormat">
             <enum>Qt::TextFormat::RichText</enum>
            </property>
            <property name="wordWrap">
             <bool>true</bool>
            </property>
            <property name="variant" stdset="0">
             <string notr="true">help</string>
            </property>
           </widget>
          </item>
